<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73417" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅμ-αυλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>living together, companion,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ὅμαυλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1083
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1.8
			</span></i> (Satyric drama), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>neighbouring,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ὅ. χθόνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					24.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλός</span>) <i>playing together on the flute,
				sounding together in concert,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					187
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
